<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 58 0 R/Alt(Block diagram of three sub-modules arranged left to right: Input Memory (parameters WIDTH, R, C, K), mac_pipe (parameters WIDTH, ACCW), and Output FIFO (parameters WIDTH, DEPTH). On the far left, the top-level input AXI-Stream signals (INPUT_TDATA labeled WIDTH, INPUT_TUSER labeled S_BITS+8, INPUT_TVALID, INPUT_TREADY) point into Input Memory. On the far right, the Output FIFO's OUT_AXIS_TDATA, OUT_AXIS_TVALID point out to the top-level OUTPUT_TDATA and OUTPUT_TVALID, and OUTPUT_TREADY points in to OUT_AXIS_TREADY. Between the blocks, several signals (including X_read_addr, X_data, W_read_addr, W_data, inputs_loaded, init_acc, compute_finished, and the FIFO's IN_AXIS_* signals) are drawn only partially connected or left dangling. A note at the bottom states that clock and reset are applied to all three components but are simplified in the drawing.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block/BBox[72 114.88757 540 241.2544]>>]/K[66]/Pg 658 0 R>>
